{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/gingham\/licensing"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/Licensing","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Free up to 10,000 rows a table; a license key shows every row."}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHLicense","doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHLicenseInfo","doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHLicenseKeyError"],"title":"License Keys","anchor":"License-Keys"}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Gingham"}],"title":"Licensing","role":"collectionGroup","roleHeading":"API Collection"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Gingham is free for any use, commercial too: each table shows up to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHLicense\/freeRowLimit","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" (10,000) rows of its data source. A table with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"more shows the first 10,000 and a notice under them (“Gingham shows the first","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"10,000 of 25,000 rows. More need a license key.”). Everything else works on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the rows it shows: sorting, filters, search, totals, copy and export. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"limit counts the data source’s rows (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"numberOfRows(in:)"},{"text":"), before filters and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"searches hide any.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A license key shows them all. Register it once, at launch, before a table","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"shows rows; tables that already show the first rows read them all again:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["import Gingham","","@main","final class AppDelegate: NSObject, NSApplicationDelegate {","    func applicationDidFinishLaunching(_ notification: Notification) {","        GHLicense.register(\"GH1.eyJidW5kbGVzIjpb…\")","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The key is checked on the device, without the network. It names the apps it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is for (their bundle identifiers, or a prefix such as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"com.example.*"},{"text":") and a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"major version of Gingham: a key for 1.x works with every 1.x release.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHLicense\/status-swift.type.property","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" tells what it gives: ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHLicense\/Status-swift.enum\/licensed(_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with the key’s ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHLicenseInfo","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":", or ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHLicense\/Status-swift.enum\/invalid(_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the reason (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHLicenseKeyError","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":"): another app, another major version, an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"expired trial. The console says it too (subsystem “Gingham”, category","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"“License”), and tells when a table first comes near the limit and when one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"first keeps to it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"While the limit cuts a table’s rows, the app’s row indexes past the first","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"10,000 aren’t the table’s: inserts, removes and moves of rows read the rows","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"again instead of moving them, so the table never shows a row it doesn’t have.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"See LICENSING.md for keys, trials and open-source apps.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"kind":"article","seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GettingStarted","doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/IntegratingIntoAnApp","doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/MigratingFromNSTableView","doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/UsingSwiftUI","doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/ReleaseNotes","doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView","doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableViewDataSource","doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableViewDelegate"],"title":"Essentials","generated":true,"anchor":"Essentials"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"references":{"doc://ngtable.Gingham/documentation/Gingham/UsingSwiftUI":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/UsingSwiftUI","title":"Using Gingham in SwiftUI","kind":"article","role":"collectionGroup","url":"\/documentation\/gingham\/usingswiftui","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Show rows in SwiftUI like with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Table"},{"type":"text","text":", with Gingham’s speed and features."}]},"doc://ngtable.Gingham/documentation/Gingham/GHTableView":{"navigatorTitle":[{"tex